  "scientific_conclusion": "Empirical evaluation on genuine CSE-CIC-IDS2018 future-day flows confirms that the supervised Random Forest suffers catastrophic recall collapse on unseen attack families (Botnet detection=0.04%, Infiltration detection=3.44%). The unsupervised Isolation Forest trained on early benign traffic substantially improves detection of unseen behavioral attacks (50.02% Botnet, 28.30% Infiltration), but temporal concept drift in benign traffic causes a higher False Positive Rate (39.39%) and constrains aggregate ROC-AUC (0.4976). Anomaly detection must function as a triage/alerting layer rather than an unconstrained autonomous blocker."
